{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FinCases","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells"],"declarations":32,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_eq_card_eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_eq_card_eigen","kind":"theorem","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L370-L379","doc":"**`gbDepth λ` is the number of distinct JM eigenvalues on the `λ`-block** —\nconditional on `SeminormalEigenvalue`.\n\nThis is the partition side of bean `wpdb` said entirely inside the algebra: no\ndiagram, no hook, no cell. It is *not* the bridge — the word side is still\nunrelated to it — but it is the shape the word side would have to match, and it\nlocalises the whole remaining partition-side debt in one named open class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.card_eigen_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.card_eigen_image","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L358-L368","doc":"The `λ`-block carries as many distinct JM eigenvalues as `λ` has contents.\n\nPure consequence of injectivity — the eigenvalue map does not collapse any two\ndiagonals — so nothing about `H_n(q)` is smuggled in beyond the class fields. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eigen","kind":"def","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L355-L356","doc":"The Jucys–Murphy eigenvalue attached to a cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalEigenvalue.eigenOfContent_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalEigenvalue.eigenOfContent_injective","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L351-L351","doc":"At generic `q` the assignment `c ↦ q^{2c}` separates contents. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalEigenvalue.eigenOfContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalEigenvalue.eigenOfContent","kind":"def","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L349-L349","doc":"The eigenvalue `L_k` acts by, as a function of the added cell's content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalEigenvalue.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalEigenvalue.mk","kind":"ctor","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L347-L347","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalEigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalEigenvalue","kind":"class","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L333-L351","doc":"**The seminormal eigenvalue theorem, carried as a §3b-cond hypothesis.**\n\nThe content is: the Jucys–Murphy element `L_k` acts on the seminormal basis of\nthe `λ`-block by a scalar depending only on the content of the cell added at\nstep `k` — `q^{2c}` in the QOU convention — and that assignment is injective at\ngeneric `q`. This is **not proved in the corpus**: `QJucysMurphy.lean` records it\nas an open GAP (Ref: [ram1997] Thm 4.1, [murphy1992], [hoefsmit1974]).\n\nPer §3b-cond the class carries the *hypotheses*, never the conclusion. The two\nfields are the eigenvalue assignment and its injectivity; `card_eigen_image`\nbelow **derives** the count from them rather than asserting it. Discharging this\nclass is option A of bean `wpdb` and would make the results downstream of it\nunconditional; it is deliberately left without an instance, which is the honest\nrepresentation of an open statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.card_content_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.card_content_image","kind":"theorem","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L320-L329","doc":"**The GB-depth counts the *distinct contents* `λ` carries.**\n\nStated on the image rather than on the extremes, because that is the form the\nalgebra side has to match: the JM eigenvalues are a *set*, one per content, and\nwhat a bridge would have to reproduce is its cardinality. See\n`card_eigen_image` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.content_image_eq_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.content_image_eq_range","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L285-L318","doc":"The contents of `λ` are exactly the integers `j - (λ'₁ - 1)` for\n`0 ≤ j < gbDepth λ` — an unbroken interval, no gaps.\n\nBoth inclusions are cheap and neither is vacuous. Forward: every cell's content\nlies between `-(λ'₁-1)` and `λ₁-1` because its row and column lengths are\ndominated by the corner's. Backward: a non-negative target is hit by a cell of\nthe *first row* and a negative one by a cell of the *first column*, and the\nbound `j < λ₁+λ'₁-1` is exactly what puts the witness inside the diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_eq_content_spread","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_eq_content_spread","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L269-L283","doc":"**The GB-depth counts the diagonals `λ` meets.**\n\n`gbDepth μ = (max content − min content) + 1`. Since the contents of a Young\ndiagram fill the whole range between their extremes — the first row supplies\n`0 … λ₁-1` and the first column `-(λ'₁-1) … 0` — this is exactly the number of\ndistinct contents.\n\nThis is the same number as the corner hook, said in the algebra's coordinates\nrather than the diagram's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_ne_on_H4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_ne_on_H4","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L219-L227","doc":"**At `n = 4` the partition grading has at least two strata.**\n\nThe counterpart to `gbDepth_const_on_H3`: the grading is degenerate at `n = 3`\nand non-degenerate at `n = 4`. That is what makes `n = 4` the first place any\ncandidate word-side filtration can be tested against it — and, via\n`WordFiltrationObstruction`, the first place the naive ideal-power reading is\nprovably not it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_p22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_p22","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L213-L217","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_p4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_p4","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L207-L211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.p22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.p22","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L203-L205","doc":"The self-conjugate `(2,2)` cell — the one the compute script flags as where\nthe two filtrations were observed to disagree. Corner hook `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.p4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.p4","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L199-L201","doc":"Two partitions of `4`, chosen because this is where the grading first\nseparates: `[4]` has corner hook `4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_const_on_H3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_const_on_H3","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L180-L197","doc":"**At `n = 3` the partition grading has exactly one stratum.**\n\nAll three `H₃` blocks have GB-depth `3`, so `Z(H₃) = Z^(3)` and every other\nstratum is zero.\n\nThe downstream consequence is the point. `conj:phi-q-categorical-truncation`\nsets `k⋆(T_w) := max {gbDepth λ : λ ∈ supp(T_w)}` and states that the\ntruncation depth is *\"structurally locked to the NF support of `T_w`\"*. At\n`n = 3` that maximum is `3` for **every** `T_w` with nonempty support — it is\nconstant, so it locks onto nothing. Whatever the truncation claim is worth at\nthe single-nucleon level, it is not carried by the support.\n\nScope-(a): this says the grading is degenerate here, not that the truncation\nis false. It becomes non-trivial from `n = 4`, where `(2,2)` has depth `3`\nagainst `4` for the four hooks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_p111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_p111","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L175-L178","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_p21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_p21","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L170-L173","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_p3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_p3","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L165-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.p111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.p111","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L163-L163","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.p21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.p21","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L162-L162","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.p3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.p3","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L159-L161","doc":"The three partitions of `3` — the `H₃` Wedderburn blocks of a single\nnucleon (`schur-weyl-mass-decomposition`: symmetric, standard, antisymmetric). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.four_le_card_of_mem_one_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.four_le_card_of_mem_one_one","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L122-L134","doc":"A diagram that is not a hook — one containing `(1,1)` — has at least four\ncells. So every partition of `n ≤ 3` is a hook, which is what makes the\n`H₃` computation below come out constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_eq_of_border_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_eq_of_border_eq","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L112-L120","doc":"**The grading is blind to the interior.** Two diagrams sharing a first row\nand a first column have the same GB-depth however differently they are shaped\nbelow and to the right of the corner — an immediate consequence of\n`gbDepth_eq_corner`, and the reason the stratification is coarse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_eq_corner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_eq_corner","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L92-L110","doc":"**The GB-depth is the corner hook**, `λ₁ + λ'₁ - 1`.\n\nThe maximum over all cells is attained at `(0,0)`: rows and columns are\nantitone, so every cell's arm and leg are dominated by the corner's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge.bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge.bridge","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L64-L64","doc":"**The conjecture** (depth-lift dichotomy, from the manuscript):\na self-conjugate cell ($\\mu^\\top = \\mu$) lifts to depth $2$ (real /\nBloch–Wigner period), a chiral pair to depth $3$ (Tate-twisted\nperiod), and every other cell's lift is bounded by its concrete\nGB-depth `gbDepth μ` (max hook length). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge.isChiralPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge.isChiralPair","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Predicate selecting the depth-3 chiral-pair period family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge.dII","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge.dII","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L56-L56","doc":"Iterated-integral depth-lift $d_{\\mathrm{II}}(\\lambda)$ of the\ncentral idempotent $e_\\lambda$ (the grouplike side). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge","kind":"class","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L48-L67","doc":"**Two-filtration bridge** (iterated-integral depth $\\leftrightarrow$\npartition-cellular GB-depth via $e_\\lambda$).\n\nConjectural class — see\n[`conj:two-filtration-bridge`](../../../quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/two-filtration-bridge.md). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:two-filtration-bridge","label":"conj:two-filtration-bridge","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/two-filtration-bridge.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L41-L46","doc":"**Partition-cellular GB-depth** $\\mathrm{depth}_{\\mathrm{GB}}(\\lambda)\n= \\max_\\square h(\\square)$: the maximum hook length over all cells\n(the centre $Z(H_n(q))$ side of the bridge). The empty diagram has\ndepth `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge.hookLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge.hookLength","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwoFiltrationBridge.lean#L35-L39","doc":"**Hook length** of cell `c = (i, j)` in a Young diagram `μ`:\narm `(rowLen i - j)` + leg `(colLen j - i)` − 1. For a cell of `μ`\nthis is `≥ 1` (truncated ℕ subtraction is exact there). ","signatureChunk":0}]}